## Added
* Rock mill
  * Earlygame post-steel crusher type machine
  * Can grind down various stones, gravel and sand into finer items while yielding byproduct
  * Mainly intended to serve as an easy way to automate/bulk craft certain elements in earlygame before BOP
  * While the byproduct chances are rather low and the recipe times are slow, the mills are easily scalable due to their low cost
  * Comes with convenient stacking frame
  * Ideal for skyblock/seablock type challenge runs, as it can be configured to serve as an Ex Nihilo substitute
  * Can also perform the sand and colloid to clay recipe of the acidizer, but at a lower efficiency
* Supercomputer
  * Does recipes involving data drives
  * Can calculate flight paths for orbital rockets and particle simulation data for fusion reactors
  * Can also process flight data which can be received from satellites
  * Most recipes have multiple variants with different cooling options
  * More expensive cooling makes the recipes faster, but more likely to fail
  * Can also create blueprint booklets without the aid of pufferfish, the recipe takes longer and much more energy, but has double the success chance
  * Can also create Klaus
* Space laboratory
  * New satellite that can provide data for drives
  * By default, can produce flight data which has to be written to a drive using a drive enclosure
  * The drive enclosure has to be placed onto one of the ground station's ports to receive data, which happens automatically if drive data is available
  * Accepts sensor relays, which produces orbital data
    * A single relay takes 100 hours to produce one drive worth of orbital data, this can be sped up by installing more relays on the same satellite
    * Time taken scales linearly, a satellite with 100 sensor relays only takes one hour per data drive

## Changed
* Updated russian localization
* The cargo elevator can now be controlled using RoR, allowing the platform to stop at certain heights
* Updated the pepperbox textures
  * The wood now looks more like wood and less like plastic
  * The bronze parts now have more depth
* Conveyor items being deleted due to cramming can now be configured with the server config `CONVEYOR_CRAM_MAX`, the default still being 25
* Conveyor belts being destroyed due to item cramming can now be configured with the server config `CONVEYOR_CRAM_EXPLODE`, it is still on by default
* Conveyor items will no longer break any belts, even with the config enabled, if the conveyor item entities have existed for less than one cram check cycle
  * This means that items that have piled up due to chunk loading should now safely self-destruct without breaking conveyor lines
* QMAW now has a composing feature, using double curly brackets and the internal name of another page, this page's contents can be imported
  * This means that things like long "see also" lists can now be on a single shared page instead of being hand written for every article
* QMAW links for pages you're already on now have a special color
* The relay satellite can now send RoR signals to different dimensions
  * It can only send, not receive. For bidirectional communication, two satellites are necessary, one in each dimension
* Fake player entities can no longer use empty blood or xp bags
* Repairing old lanterns now grants vending machine tokens, with the amount of tokens representing the player's reputation (always at least 1, so negative rep is not shown)
* The soyuz and related recipes no longer need blueprints in normal mode, instead they use flight simulation data from the supercomputer
* The PUREX now has a sound loop
* The PWR's coolant type can no longer be changed if fuel is loaded
* RBMK steam channels and heat exchangers can no longer have their coolant type changed if the column temperature exceeds 50°C and the input buffer has fluid in it
  * This means that RBMK columns remain configurable if added to an already hot reactor, right until the input accepts fluid
* Satellite ground stations now display some more detailed information about the connected satellite, like the type and cooldown for orbital weapons
* Satellite item descriptions now use translation keys
* The centrifuge's item IO now only allows valid centrifugable items to be inserted
* Removed the reactor remote control's recipe
* Quadrupled the yield of helium-3 from moon turf, making it easier to make sustained helium-3 reactors
* The ground station now has OpenComputers integration, as well as an RoR value that returns the satellite type
* The ZIRNOX now has RoR integration allowing to select a monitor slot, which can provide values about the rod's type and depletion value
* The pile now has thorium-232 rods which can be bred into thorium fuel
* Updated yharonite billet texture
* Item magnet armor mods are now 50% stronger
* Meteors can now be detected by radar and radar satellites
* Meteors, artillery shells and artillery rockets can now be destroyed by damage with an "energy" type (lasers, plasma) exceeding 250 points
  * This means that the orbital precision laser can now intercept these entities
* Updated the automatic thresher
  * Nether wart, pumpkins and melons can now be harvested
  * Pumpkin and melon stems are now ignored
* The liquefactor and solidifier recipe time has been reduced from 5 seconds to 3 seconds
* Melons can now be directly liquefacted into ethanol
* Liquefacting coal and lignite now yields significantly more coal oil in order to compete with coal oil from the combination oven
* Added the server config `ULTRA_LARP_MODE`
  * If enabled, most large doors can no longer be operated manually
  * The exception bein the water door due to it having two large hand-operated cranks
* Retextured the grenade fuze items so that the fuze type remains visible even with the stack size number enabled
* The remnants power armor is now made in the precision assembler using discoverable blueprints
* Increased RPA resistance against physical, fire and energy damage types
* The satellite cargo pad no longer auto-pushes items out of its inventory
* The satellite cargo pad now uses the current multiblock system, existing pads should convert automatically
* The pyrolysis oven no longer requires fullerite (except in expensive mode)
* Updated the model of the cargo landing pad as well as the drop ship
  * The drop ship now brakes before landing, and now has landing struts which are extended
  * The drop ship no longer fires its thrusters when landed, which means it no longer spams particles
* The soyuz landing capsule can now be emptied via hoppers
* Changed the recipe of the flow control pump

## Fixed
* Fixed pollution detector localization not working, showing only error messages instead of the pollution type names
* Fixed un-clamped gaussian random use on the wideband detector satellite, causing uncommon detections with inaccuracy exceeding the intended amount
* Fixed PSN bulk storage duping itself when broken
* Fixed old lantern repair bonus not being applied when the player is too far away from the lantern or another player is in the detection area
* Fixed an issue where the vast majority of fluid spilling machines would ignore all fluid trait spill actions except for the soot/poison polluting ones
* Fixed a potential issue regarding bobblehead world generation
* The powered condenser now has a bit more tolerance with its power consumption, preventing edge cases where due to power grid limitations in certain circumstances, the power requirement can never be met
* Fixed gamebreaking issue where the tooltip of the RoR terminal was misspelled
* Fixed RoR pager only having a max channel length of 10 instead of 15
* Power armor fall sounds no longer trigger for falls 0.5m or less, hopefully fixing an issue where using cargo elevators would repeatedly trigger the fall sound
* Fixed PRISM system blast resistance checks supplying incorrect position info to blocks for the resistance getter
* Fixed lunar miner not requiring the orbital module
* Fixed issue with the counter valve not accounting for the final tick of transfer, letting too much fluid pass
* Fixed bauxite bedrock ore fragments not being able to be crafted into anything
* Fixed issue where the collisions of the RoR panel blocks didn't work right
* Fixed balefire thruster custom missile part not having any recipes, and the shortened thruster having two
* Fixed assembly factory and chemical factory RoR reader index offset
* Item entities affected by magnets are now forced to send velocity updates, fixing a desync in multiplayer with magnet armor mods
* Fixed long size 10 custom missile fuselages not being obtainable due to incorrectly set up recipes yielding the short variants instead
* Fixed white crayon being uncraftable
* Fixed solidifier and liquefactor not saving their power and progress to NBT
* Fixed orbital precision laser dealing no damage due to a quirk in the explosion VNT code
* Pneumatic networks can no longer send items to the source inventory in a loop, fixing an issue where doing so would delete items
* Fixed the placement preview offset for the soyuz launcher
* Fixed a bug where special revives would not work when dying from radiation, since radiation would deal fatal damage twice
* Fixed the soyuz not using interpolation when launching, causing its movement to be fixed at 20 FPS
* Fixed the soyuz landing capsule's landing position being slightly offset on negative coordinates (yes it's another coordinate truncation error)
